  "code": "// * stands for the argument the new function takes\nlet add_5 = add(5, *)\nwrite_line(\"add_5(3): {add_5(3)}\")\n\n// the fixed arguments are evaluated once, here\nwrite_line(\"add 10 to each: {[1, 2, 3] |> map(add(10, *))}\")\n\n// a built-in operator, with both operands open\nwrite_line(\"product: {[2, 3, 4] |> reduce(1, int.`*(*, *))}\")",
